<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<jmeterTestPlan version="1.2" properties="5.0" jmeter="5.6.3">
  <hashTree>
    <TestPlan guiclass="TestPlanGui" testclass="TestPlan"
              testname="Case Management — Re-accreditation Performance Tests" enabled="true">
      <stringProp name="TestPlan.comments">Performance test — re-accreditation work-item lifecycle journeys.
No pre-seeding: this plan discovers its own work items over HTTP at run time.

Rewritten for app template v12 (RA-410 removed the task-checklist model and the
withdraw-from-case-management journey; RA-291/RA-337 replaced it with duly-make
-> self-assign -> log-decision, plus a standalone query endpoint). See
case-management-frontend's src/server/work-items/re-accreditation/module.js for
the authoritative flow.

Work-item discovery (no CSV files, no seeding step): a Setup Thread Group runs
once before the 3 worker groups, stub-logs in (nation left blank, so it can see
every nation's items), then pages through
GET /work-items?status=submitted&amp;assigneeMode=any&amp;filtersApplied=1 (the
"Not started" status filter with the "Your applications" assignee filter removed) to
collect every currently-available work item id via regex on its state-tag
data-testid. Those ids are shuffled and split ~40/30/30 into three
ConcurrentLinkedQueue instances stored in JMeter's cross-thread-group `props`
store (cmsApproveQueue/cmsRefuseQueue/cmsQueryQueue). Each worker thread group
has a JSR223PreProcessor in place of the old CSVDataSet that polls its own
queue once per loop iteration and sets ${workItemId}; an empty queue throws
JMeterStopThreadException, so a thread stops cleanly (same end-of-work
behaviour CSVDataSet's stopThread=true used to give) once its share is drained.
This makes the plan self-contained and portable — it works against ANY
environment (local, perf-test, ...) using whatever real "Not started" work
items already exist there, without any pre-extraction step or environment-
specific CSV data.

Because discovered items are ones the app itself marked "Not started"
(genuine submissions via epr-register-enrol-frontend/accreditation-reprocessor
or accreditation-exporter, not ones created by directly POSTing to case-
management's own create-work-item form), each one has a real linked operator
application. That matters for the final decision step: case-management-
backend's "Log decision" push to the operator-facing backend only succeeds for
items with a real linked application, so approve/refuse reach genuine terminal
states here (verified previously via a matching, manually-chained local run —
68 approved / 10 rejected reached real terminal states), unlike work items
seeded directly via case-management's own create form.

Load profile: 10 concurrent users (4+3+3 across the 3 worker-pool thread
groups), ramping over 1s to match epr-re-ex-admin-fe-perf-tests' own
ThreadGroup config (num_threads=10, ramp_time=1, verified directly against
that repo's scenarios/epr-admin-fe-test.jmx) — effectively a near-instant
burst to full concurrency rather than a staged ramp.

Thread Groups (10 users total, ramped over 1s):
  1. Approval  (4 threads) draining the discovered approve queue (~40% of found items)
     duly-make -> self-assign (auto: duly-made -> assessment-in-progress) -> decision=approved
  2. Refusal   (3 threads) draining the discovered refuse queue (~30% of found items)
     duly-make -> self-assign -> decision=rejected
  3. Query     (3 threads) draining the discovered query queue (~30% of found items)
     query (submitted -> queried) via the query-during-duly-making transition
Total: 10 workers at peak (4+3+3), reached in ~1s; actual throughput is capped
by however many "Not started" items are available at discovery time — if fewer
than 10 are found, some threads stop immediately with nothing queued for them.
on_sample_error=continue on each worker group so one item's failure doesn't
stop that worker from picking up its next queued item.</stringProp>
      <boolProp name="TestPlan.functional_mode">false</boolProp>
      <boolProp name="TestPlan.tearDown_on_shutdown">false</boolProp>
      <boolProp name="TestPlan.serialize_threadgroups">false</boolProp>
